<Base title="Privacy Policy | Tidewater" description="How Tidewater Advisory LLC intends to handle information submitted through its bid desk, newsletter and contact forms.">
<section class="section"><div class="container article"><p class="eyebrow">Legal</p><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p class="fine">Effective date: [[TODO: Launch date]] · [[TODO: Legal review and approval before publication]]</p><h2>Who we are</h2><p>Tidewater is a trade name of Tidewater Advisory LLC. We operate a government bid information and advisory website. Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@tidewaterbid.com">hello@tidewaterbid.com</a>. Mailing address: [[TODO: Business mailing address]].</p><h2>Information we collect</h2><p>When you contact us, request a bid packet, take the readiness check or subscribe, we collect the information you submit. That may include name, business, email, phone, service categories and locations, coverage and registration status, staffing, answers and readiness score, the bid requested, consent timestamps and messages.</p><h2>How we use it</h2><p>We use submitted details to respond to your request, assess potential bid matches, operate the bid desk and send emails only within the scope of your consent. Newsletter signups require a confirmation email before subscription.</p><h2>Service providers</h2><p>Airtable stores form submissions. Cloudflare hosts the site and processes form requests. [[TODO: Confirm email provider — implementation supports Resend.]] Optional privacy-friendly analytics may be provided by Plausible, without reverse-IP identification by Tidewater. Review these providers' policies before launch.</p><h2>Retention and access</h2><p>[[TODO: Publish retention period, deletion process and any legal retention exceptions.]] Contact <a href="mailto:hello@tidewaterbid.com">hello@tidewaterbid.com</a> to request correction or deletion, subject to legal obligations.</p><h2>Email choices</h2><p>Marketing emails include a way to unsubscribe. Unsubscribing stops future marketing messages; you may still receive necessary replies to a direct request.</p><h2>Cookies and tracking</h2><p>The site may store a local preference for light or dark appearance and an in-session headline-test assignment. It does not use visitor IP reversal or advertising retargeting in v1. [[TODO: Recheck all deployed third-party scripts and analytics settings.]]</p><h2>Security and changes</h2><p>We use server-side credentials for external systems. No internet service is perfectly secure. We may update this policy; the current version will appear on this page.</p></div></section>
</Base>
